{
	"comment": "Shared conformance vectors for the access model's permission decision: engine/server/accesschain.go (accessChains.holds) and client/src/access.ts (canAt) must reach the same verdict on every case both can decide. A caller holds a permission at a row when it holds it at the workspace root, at the row itself, or at any row up the row's chain of access parents. `access` maps each permission the caller holds to where: `root` for the workspace root, `anchors` as entity name to row keys; null means no summary has reached the client, which only the client can be missing. `chain` lists the rows above the row, nearest first: the row its access_parent names, the row that row's access_parent names, and so on, until a row whose entity has no access parent or whose reference is unset. A chain that ends in the string \"unknown\" stops at a row the client does not hold, which the server never lacks. `want` is \"yes\", \"no\" or \"unknown\"; the engine checks the cases whose `access` is not null and whose `chain` holds no \"unknown\", where \"yes\" means it holds the permission.",
